# What you type at the shell. The flag list is read from `claude --help` on the
# build you actually have, so it moves when the CLI does; the groups below are
# the handful worth knowing by heart.
name:    claude
what:    Claude Code from the shell — starting, resuming, and one-shot runs
check:   claude
docs:    claude --help
probe:   help

= STARTING — and not losing yesterday's work
claude           | new session here
claude -c        | continue the most recent conversation. Aliased to `ccc`
claude --resume  | pick an older session from a list. Aliased to `ccr`
claude --fork-session | resume, but branch instead of overwriting
claude -p "..."  | one question, answer printed, no session. Good in pipes
claude --add-dir DIR | let it read a second directory outside this one

= IN THE BACKGROUND
claude --bg      | start in the background and hand back the prompt
@claude attach   | pull a background session into this terminal
@claude agents   | list background sessions

= WHICH MODEL AM I ACTUALLY GETTING
omniroute-where  | the base URL and both combos, from shell/common.sh
claude --model X | override for one session
--fallback-model | switch automatically if the first one errors

= FLAGS WORTH KNOWING ABOUT
--dangerously-skip-permissions | no approval prompts. Know why before using it
--allowed-tools  | permit specific tools without prompting
--effort         | reasoning effort for this session
--bare           | skip hooks, LSP and plugins. For diagnosing a slow start
--debug          | show what it is doing under the hood

= ALL FLAGS (from --help)
